target: internal/push/push.go
verify: go test ./internal/push/ -count=1 -run 'TestTheTierDoesNotReachTheGate'
expect: tier_executed changed the push decision
why:    the push gate does not read the tier — a `partial` run pushes on its convergence and outcome like any other, and the PR report is where the tier is shown. Ported from the skills catalog's push-gate-reads-the-tier when push-check.py was retired: five places in the Python's docs once claimed the gate read the tier, and prose about what another module reads has no failing assertion when it rots. This entry is that assertion.
--- old
	var outcome string
	if r.Finish != nil {
		outcome = r.Finish.Outcome
	}
--- new
	var outcome string
	if r.Finish != nil {
		outcome = r.Finish.Outcome
		if r.Finish.TierExecuted == "partial" {
			return Result{Push: false, Reason: "the run was only partially reviewed", Convergence: conv}, nil
		}
	}
